{"abstract":"We present a Research through Design exploration of the potential for using tangible and embodied interactions to enable active music experiences - musicking - for non-musicians. We present the Tubularium prototype, which aims to facilitate music-making to non-musicians by not requiring any initial skill while still eliciting agency and overall, providing a meaningful experience. We present the design of the prototype and the features implemented and reflect on insights from a public event in which the prototype was trialed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Montesinos Garcia, Lucia","Jensen, Halfdan Hauch","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818255"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Embodied interaction","Musicking","Non Musicians","Research through Design","Tangible interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enabling embodied music making for non musicians","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15699662","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818255","identifier":[{"id":"105010843977","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f4b27c41-80c3-4a4f-aa9b-41866214f073"],"keyword":["Embodied Interaction","Musicking","Non-Musicians","Research through Design","Tangible Interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3A6964F02285C03B092FBC3AF383CD4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15699662","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucía","key":"montesínospau","last":"Montesínos","locid":"8999b149-c410-4fd7-882f-9be2e31a4fe8","name":"Montesinos Garcia, Lucia","name_org":"Montesínos, Lucía","orcid":"0009-0002-1438-6461","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Halfdan Hauch","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"82a68906-d29e-47d3-9b30-ab8c6e916283","name":"Jensen, Halfdan Hauch","orcid":"0000-0002-0351-6489","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","name_org":"Løvlie, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.15699662","pages":"1-7","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on New Interfaces for Musical Expression"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010843977"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f4b27c41-80c3-4a4f-aa9b-41866214f073"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enabling Embodied Music-Making for Non-Musicians","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818255","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a Research through Design exploration of the potential for using tangible interactions to enable active music experiences - musicking - for non-musicians. We present the Tubularium prototype, which aims to help non-musicians play music without requiring any initial skill. We present the initial design of the prototype and the features implemented in order to enable music-making by non-musicians, and offer some reflections based on observations of informal initial user explorations of the prototype.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Montesinos Garcia, Lucia","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Jensen, Halfdan Hauch"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747259"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Music","Musicking","Research through Design","Tangible interactions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using tangible interaction to design musicking artifacts for non musicians","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2404.09597.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747259","ids":["itu-b7531ccc-7d89-43cd-b9ea-63cdc1b8838c"],"keyword":["Music","Musicking","Research through Design","tangible interactions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-01AACD3125C7F80F7B2536C2ABE3431D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.09597","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2404.09597.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucia","key":"montesinosgarciapau","last":"Montesinos Garcia","locid":"8999b149-c410-4fd7-882f-9be2e31a4fe8","name":"Montesinos Garcia, Lucia","orcid":"0009-0002-1438-6461","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Halfdan Hauch","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"82a68906-d29e-47d3-9b30-ab8c6e916283","name":"Jensen, Halfdan Hauch","orcid":"0000-0002-0351-6489","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b7531ccc-7d89-43cd-b9ea-63cdc1b8838c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using Tangible Interaction to Design Musicking Artifacts for Non-musicians","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747259","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Atrial Fibrillation Better Care (ABC) pathway was proposed for a more integrated atrial fibrillation (AF) care. We investigated if adherence to the ABC pathway was associated to the quality of anticoagulation control in a cohort of AF outpatients starting vitamin K antagonists (VKAs) between July 2016 and June 2018. Patients were considered adherent to the ABC pathway if they met all of its components. The time in therapeutic range (TTR) was estimated at one year. In total, 1045 patients (51.6% female; median age 77 years; 63% ABC pathway adherent) were included. At one year, 474 (51.6%) of 919 patients with international normalized ratio (INR) data for TTR estimation had a TTR &lt; 65%. Among ABC pathway non-adherent patients, a greater proportion had TRT &lt; 65% (56.4% vs. 43.6%, p = 0.025), and TTR &lt; 70% (64.9% vs. 35.1%, p = 0.033), with lower mean TTR in non-adherent patients (59.4 ± 22.3% vs. 63.9 ± 21.1%; p = 0.004). Logistic regression models demonstrated that the ABC pathway adherence in its continuous (aOR: 0.75, 95% CI 0.59-0.96) and categorical (aOR: 0.75, 95% CI 0.57-0.98) forms was independently associated with TTR ≥ 65%. In this 'real-world' cohort of AF patients starting VKAs, the ABC pathway adherent patients had better TTR, and more ABC criteria fulfilled increased the probability of achieving good TTR.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Roldán, Vanessa","Martínez-Montesinos, Lorena","López-Gálvez, Raquel","García-Tomás, Lucía","Lip, Gregory Y H","Rivera-Caravaca, José Miguel","Marín, Francisco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-097693"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rivera-Caravaca, José Miguel"],"country":["Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red (CIBER)","Hospital Morales Meseguer","Hospital Virgen de la Arrixaca","Instituto Murciano de Investigación Biosanitaria","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","University of Liverpool","University of Murcia"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Time in therapeutic range","vitamin K antagonists"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relation of the atrial fibrillation better care abc pathway to the quality of anticoagulation in atrial fibrillation patients taking vitamin k antagonists","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jpm12030487","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-097693","identifier":[{"id":"35330486","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85127384054","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8954236","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-a4447eef-a2b6-455e-b052-eebd79682743"],"keyword":["Atrial Fibrillation Better Care (ABC) pathway","atrial fibrillation","time in therapeutic range","vitamin K antagonists"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59EB0DC13F1C43F1E3B7E17EAB6BD78A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jpm12030487","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/466416453/Rold_n_et_al._2022_._Relation_of_the_Atrial_Fibrillation_Better_Care_ABC_Pathway_to_the_Quality_of_Anticoagulation_in_Atrial_Fibrillation_Patients_Taking_Vitamin_K_Antagonists.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"es","key":"university of murcia","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Murcia","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"hospital morales meseguer","l